          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#original_version_for_associative_algebras Original version for associative algebras
          %p
            The
            %strong formality theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kontsevich97"}> Kontsevich 97
            ) states that there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E-algebra"} L-∞-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polyvector+fields"} polyvector fields
            (with zero differential and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schouten-Nijenhuis+bracket"} Schouten-Nijenhuis bracket
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
            of the shifted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cochain complex
            (with Hochschild differential and Gerstenhaber bracket), whose first Taylor coefficient is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild-Kostant-Rosenberg+theorem"} HKR
            quasi-isomorphism.
          %p
            Tamarkin alternatively proves the formality of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+disks+operad"} little disks operad
            (see also Kontsevich 1999) and proves that it implies the Kontsevich formality.
          %p
            The Kontsevich formality theorem implies that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+infinity-group"} automorphism infinity-group
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E1-operad"} E1-operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck-Teichm%C3%BCller+group"} Grothendieck-Teichmüller group
            (see there for more).
          %h3#GeneralVersionForEnAlgebras
            General version for higher
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
          %p
            More generally, a result of Kontsevich and Tamarkin (…) says that over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            0 the canonical functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi Algebras
                    %mi 𝔽
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi Algebras
                    %mi 𝔽
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_n Algebras_{\mathbb{F}}
                  \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  P_n Algebras_{\mathbb{F}}
          %p
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-n+algebras"} E-n algebras
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+n-algebras"} Poisson n-algebras
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            (since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
            %em
              The
              = succeed "\u201C" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
            over a field of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+little+n-disk+operad+is+formal"} the little n-disk operad is formal
          %p
            But of course the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+infinity-group"} automorphism infinity-group
            of both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_n
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_n
            acts on both sides and makes the space of all possible such equivalences a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            over this group. A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_n
            algebra may be thought of as encoding a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            of higher dimension, of sorts, and so formality says that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
            of a prequantum field theory always exists and that the choices are being acted on by the corresponding higher analog of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck-Teichm%C3%BCller+group"} Grothendieck-Teichmüller group
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"}> deformation quantization
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck-Teichm%C3%BCller+group"} Grothendieck-Teichmüller group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+little+n-disk+operad+is+formal"} the little n-disk operad is formal
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "Hochschild+cohomology#DifferentialCalculus"}> Hochschild cohomology – Differential calculus
                \.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Kontsevich97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation quantization of Poisson manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9709040"} q-alg/9709040
                %strong 66
                (2003), no. 3, 157–216
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1023/B:MATH.0000027508.00421.bf"} doi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Operads and motives in deformation quantization
                %strong 48
                (1999), no. 1, 35–72.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Tamarkin"}> Dmitry Tamarkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Another proof of M. Kontsevich formality theorem
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9803025"} math.QA/9803025
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Formality of chain operad of little discs
                %strong 66
                (1-2):65–72, 2003.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernhard+Keller"}> Bernhard Keller
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes for an Introduction to Kontsevich’s quantization theorem
                %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~bernhard.keller/publ/emalca.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Dan Petersen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Minimal models, GT-action and formality of the little disk operad
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1303.1448"} arxiv/1303.1448
            %li
              %p
                Damien Calaque, Carlo A. Rossi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on Duflo isomorphisms in Lie algebra and complex geometry
                %a{:href => "http://people.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/crossi/LectETHbook.pdf"} MPI pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tamarkin’s proof of Kontsevich’s formality theorem
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003052"} math.QA/0003052
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vasily+Dolgushev"}> Vasily Dolgushev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em All coefficients entering Kontsevich’s formality quasi-isomorphism can be replaced by rational numbers
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.6733"} arxiv/1306.6733
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Damien+Calaque"}> Damien Calaque
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Willwacher"} Thomas Willwacher
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Triviality of the higher Formality Theorem
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.4605"} arxiv/1310.4605
          %p
            In agreement with Tsygan’s philosophy of noncommutative differential calculus and its relations to braces algebra, Willwacher extends the Kontsevich formality to a homotopy braces morphism and to a
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Willwacher"}> Thomas Willwacher
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A note on Br-infinity and KS-infinity formality
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1109.3520"} arxiv/1109.3520
          %p
            Campos has extended Kontsevich formality to a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi BV
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BV_\infty
            morphism using a cyclic analog of the minimal operad
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ricardo+Campos"}> Ricardo Campos
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em BV Formality
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.07715"} arxiv/1506.07715
          .property
            category:
